.TH CLAUDE-CAGE 1 "February 2026" "claude-cage 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
claude-cage \- a sandboxed git workflow for Claude Code
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B claude-cage
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fISUBCOMMAND\fR] [\fB\-\-\fR \fIARGS\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B claude-cage
creates an isolated sandbox for Claude Code using git-based file isolation.
It creates a sanitized copy of your project (excluding sensitive files) and
uses git to sync changes back to your source repository.
.PP
Key features:
.IP \(bu 2
No sudo required \- runs as current user
.IP \(bu 2
Git-based sync with real commit history via fast-export/fast-import
.IP \(bu 2
File exclusion via :(exclude,glob) pathspec (no excluded content in intermediary)
.IP \(bu 2
Configurable history depth (default: 50 commits)
.IP \(bu 2
Network filtering via iptables (optional)
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B git-merge
Fetch refs from intermediary repository for manual merge. Use this when
autoMerge is disabled and you want to bring Claude's changes back to source.
.TP
.B clean \fR[\fIID\fR...]
Remove cached session(s). With no arguments, presents interactive selection
with an option to remove all. With one or more session IDs, removes those
specific sessions after confirmation.
.TP
.B clean \-\-all
Remove all cached sessions for the current project. Prompts for confirmation.
.TP
.B completion \fISHELL\fR
Output shell completion script for the specified shell (bash or zsh).
Can be used with eval: \fBeval "$(claude-cage completion bash)"\fR
.TP
.B install-completions
Install shell completions for the current shell. Detects whether you're
running bash or zsh and installs the appropriate completion wrapper to
your home directory. Completions are available in new shell sessions.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-test
Drop into an interactive shell for testing instead of launching the
configured command.
.TP
.B \-\-direct-mount
Mount the source directory directly into the sandbox without git sync.
Changes made inside the sandbox immediately affect source files.
.TP
.B \-\-scoped
Scope the intermediary to the current subdirectory only. Creates a
separate intermediary containing only files under the current path.
Useful for large monorepos.
.TP
.B \-\-attach-session \fR[\fITIMESTAMP\fR]
Attach to an existing active session. If a timestamp is given, attaches
to that specific session. Otherwise, auto-selects or prompts if multiple
active sessions exist.
.TP
.B \-\-all
Remove all sessions. Only valid with the \fBclean\fR subcommand.
.TP
.B \-\-dry-run
Show commands without executing them. Useful for understanding what
claude-cage will do.
.TP
.B \-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose
Show commands as they execute. Helpful for debugging.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Show full command output (implies \fB\-\-verbose\fR).
.TP
.B \-h\fR, \fB\-\-help
Display help message and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Display version number and exit.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration files are loaded and merged in order (later values override,
arrays merge):
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
/etc/claude-cage.conf              System-wide
~/.config/claude-cage/config       User
includeIf matches                  Directory-scoped (set in system/user)
.claude-cage                       Project (at git root)
.fi
.RE
.PP
Configuration uses Lua syntax:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
claude_cage {
    launch = "claude",
    mode = "bwrap",
    autoMerge = true,
    exclude = { ".env", "secrets/**" },
    networkMode = "allowlist",
    allow = {
        domains = { "github.com:443" }
    },
    git = {
        historyDepth = 50,
        blockForceAdd = true
    }
}
.fi
.RE
.SS Configuration Options
.TP
.B launch
Command to run inside sandbox (default: "claude")
.TP
.B mode
Sandbox mode: "bwrap" or "docker" (default: "bwrap")
.TP
.B autoMerge
Enable real-time sync via named pipe (default: false)
.TP
.B exclude
Array of patterns to exclude via :(exclude,glob) pathspec
.TP
.B directMount
Mount source directly without git sync (default: false)
.TP
.B allowNonGit
Allow running in non-git directories (default: unset, prompts)
.TP
.B isolated
Only mount single project instead of all same-session projects (default: false)
.TP
.B showBanner
Show ASCII banner on startup (default: true)
.TP
.B hideConfirmationPrompt
Skip the startup confirmation prompt (default: false)
.TP
.B createCagedDir
Create .caged/ symlinks to session caches (default: false)
.TP
.B additionalMounts
Extra mounts for sandbox. Each entry is a string (read-only, same path inside
sandbox) or an object with source, as/dest (optional), and mode ("ro" or "rw").
.TP
.B networkMode
Network filtering: "disabled", "allowlist", or "blocklist" (default: "disabled")
.TP
.B allow
Allowed destinations when networkMode is "allowlist"
.TP
.B block
Blocked destinations when networkMode is "blocklist"
.SS Docker Options
.TP
.B docker.image
Docker image to use (default: "node:lts-slim"). Only used when mode = "docker".
.TP
.B docker.packages
Array of packages to install in Docker container as root before dropping
privileges (default: {"curl", "iputils-ping"}). Set to empty table to skip
package installation.
.SS Git Options
.TP
.B git.historyDepth
First-parent depth on default branch (default: 50). Actual commit count may
be higher due to merge history, feature branches, and in-scope branch discovery.
.TP
.B git.defaultBranch
Default branch for history anchoring: "auto" or explicit name (default: "auto")
.TP
.B git.scoped
Always create scoped intermediary for subdirectories (default: false).
Same as using the \fB\-\-scoped\fR flag.
.TP
.B git.blockForceAdd
Block commits containing force-added gitignored files (default: true).
Override inside sandbox with: CLAUDE_CAGE_ALLOW_IGNORED=1 git commit
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CLAUDE_CAGE_CACHE
Override cache directory (default: ~/.cache/claude-cage)
.TP
.B CLAUDE_CAGE_RUNTIME
Override runtime directory (default: $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/claude-cage)
.TP
.B CLAUDE_CAGE_SESSION
Override session ID for path construction (auto-generated as YYYYMMDDHHMMSS timestamp)
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.cache/claude-cage/intermediary/<project-path>/
Shared bare repo with real commit history (git origin for work directories)
.TP
.I ~/.cache/claude-cage/scoped/<git-root>/<scope>/.bare/
Scoped bare repo for subdirectory-only intermediaries
.TP
.I ~/.cache/claude-cage/sessions/<timestamp>/work/<project-path>/
Per-session working directory where Claude operates
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/claude-cage/pipes/<timestamp>/<project-path>
Named pipes for hook communication
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/claude-cage/sessions/<path-hash>/
Session tracking (PID files)
.SH EXAMPLES
Start sandbox with configured launch command:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
claude-cage
.fi
.RE
.PP
Drop into a shell for testing:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
claude-cage --test
.fi
.RE
.PP
Pass arguments through to launch command:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
claude-cage --resume
.fi
.RE
.PP
Run in scoped mode from a subdirectory:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
cd ~/monorepo/services/api
claude-cage --scoped
.fi
.RE
.PP
Attach to an active session:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
claude-cage --attach-session
claude-cage --attach-session 20250206143022
.fi
.RE
.PP
Clean up a specific session:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
claude-cage clean 20250206143022
.fi
.RE
.PP
Clean all sessions for this project:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
claude-cage clean --all
.fi
.RE
.PP
Fetch intermediary refs for manual merge:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
claude-cage git-merge
.fi
.RE
.PP
Install shell completions:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
claude-cage install-completions
.fi
.RE
.PP
Add completions to your shell rc file:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
# In ~/.bashrc or ~/.zshrc
eval "$(claude-cage completion bash)"  # or zsh
.fi
.RE
.SH PLATFORM SUPPORT
.TP
.B Linux
Both bwrap and docker modes supported
.TP
.B Windows (WSL 2)
Both bwrap and docker modes supported
.TP
.B macOS
Docker mode only (bwrap requires Linux kernel features)
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bwrap (1),
.BR docker (1),
.BR git (1)
